== Other media ==
In September 2024, [[Marvel Comics]] announced a five-issue comic book prequel series, also titled ''Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man'', that was written by [[Christos Gage]] and features art by Eric Gapstur.<ref name="PrequelComic" /> Trammell explained that the comic fills a gap in the timeline of the series' first episode, and said it was possible that more comic books could be written to fill other timeline gaps later in the series.<ref name="PasteJan2025" /> The comic includes characters not featured in the series such as [[Silvermane|Silvio Manfredi / Silvermane]],<ref name="PrequelComic1" /> [[Crusher Hogan]],<ref name="PrequelComic2SR" /> [[Man Mountain Marko]],<ref name="PrequelComicCB" /> and the [[Enforcers (comics)|Enforcers]] members [[Jackson Brice (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Montana]], [[Fancy Dan]], and [[Ox (comics)|Ox]].<ref name="PrequelComic2CBR" /> It was published from December 11, 2024, to April 23, 2025.<ref name="PrequelComic" /><ref name="PrequelComic5" />

In September 2026, Marvel Comics announced a four-issue comic book prequel series, titled ''[[Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man Season 2 (comic)|Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man Season 2]]'', with Gage and Gapstur returning once again as writer and artist, respectively.<ref name="YFNSMS2PrequelIGN" /> Gage developed the comic in coordination with Trammell. It is set between the first and second season of the series, and introduces several members of [[List of Spider-Man enemies|Spider-Man's rogues' gallery]],<ref name="YFNSMS2PrequelCollider" /> including [[Flint Marko (Marvel Cinematic Universe)|Flint Marko / Sandman]].<ref name="YFNSMS2PrequelSandman" /> The first issue is scheduled for release on December 9.<ref name="YFNSMS2PrequelIGN" />

